      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Comaparable interface is used for natural order sorting present in java.lang.\n\n2. Buts if we want to sort in custom order we must use interface called\nComparator.\n\n3. This Comparator is present in java.util package.\n\n4 . Used in cases for sorting:\n      ->Custom sorting\n      -> java built in classes\n\n5 . it has method called compare()\n\npublic int compare(Object 1, Object 2)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Comaparable interface is used for natural order sorting present in java.lang.\n\n2. Buts if we want to sort in custom order we must use interface called\nComparator.\n\n3. This Comparator is present in java.util package.\n\n4 . Used in cases for sorting:\n      ->Custom sorting\n      -> java built in classes\n\n5 . it has method called compare()\n\npublic int compare(Object 1, Object 2)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
